---
// SpaceTechTracker.astro - Feature 4: Space Tech & Recon Satellite Tracker
---
<div class="hud-panel hud-corner space-card">
  <div class="space-header">
    <div>
      <div class="space-title-row">
        <span class="badge badge-pantone-2022">ORBITAL DEFENSE DOMAIN</span>
        <h3 class="font-mono space-heading">SPACE WARFARE & RECONNAISSANCE SATELLITE TRACKER</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="font-mono text-muted" style="font-size: 0.76rem;">Military LEO optical, SAR radar imaging constellations, SBIRS missile warning & ASAT engagement envelopes.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Orbit Domain Toggles -->
    <div class="orbit-toggles font-mono">
      <button class="orbit-btn active" data-orbit="ALL">All Altitudes</button>
      <button class="orbit-btn" data-orbit="LEO">LEO (160 - 2,000 km)</button>
      <button class="orbit-btn" data-orbit="MEO">MEO (20,200 km / PNT)</button>
      <button class="orbit-btn" data-orbit="GEO">GEO (35,786 km / Early Warning)</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="space-grid">
    <!-- Visual Orbit Stack SVG Diagram -->
    <div class="orbit-visual-box hud-panel">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 360 380" class="orbit-svg" id="orbitSvg">
        <defs>
          <radialGradient id="earthGlow" cx="50%" cy="100%" r="80%">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#6667AB" stop-opacity="0.6" />
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0E131A" stop-opacity="0.9" />
          </radialGradient>
        </defs>

        <!-- Earth Surface at Bottom -->
        <path d="M 0,380 Q 180,310 360,380 Z" fill="url(#earthGlow)" stroke="#6667AB" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="180" y="365" text-anchor="middle" fill="#FFFFFF" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">EARTH SURFACE</text>

        <!-- LEO Layer (160 - 2,000km) -->
        <path d="M 0,270 Q 180,210 360,270" fill="none" stroke="rgba(245, 223, 77, 0.4)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
        <text x="30" y="255" fill="#F5DF4D" font-family="monospace" font-size="8">LEO (OPTICAL & SAR RECON)</text>

        <!-- MEO Layer (GPS / GLONASS / BeiDou) -->
        <path d="M 0,170 Q 180,120 360,170" fill="none" stroke="rgba(102, 103, 171, 0.4)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
        <text x="30" y="155" fill="#8E8FC9" font-family="monospace" font-size="8">MEO (PNT NAVIGATION / GPS)</text>

        <!-- GEO Layer (SBIRS Missile Warning) -->
        <path d="M 0,70 Q 180,30 360,70" fill="none" stroke="rgba(255, 190, 152, 0.4)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
        <text x="30" y="55" fill="#FFBE98" font-family="monospace" font-size="8">GEO (SBIRS MISSILE EARLY WARNING)</text>

        <!-- Animated Satellites -->
        <!-- LEO Sat -->
        <g transform="translate(180, 235)" class="sat-node">
          <circle r="4" fill="#F5DF4D" />
          <line x1="-12" y1="0" x2="12" y2="0" stroke="#F5DF4D" stroke-width="2" />
          <text x="16" y="3" fill="#F5DF4D" font-family="monospace" font-size="7">USA-314 (KEYHOLE)</text>
        </g>

        <!-- LEO SAR Sat -->
        <g transform="translate(270, 255)" class="sat-node">
          <circle r="4" fill="#BB2649" />
          <line x1="-10" y1="0" x2="10" y2="0" stroke="#BB2649" stroke-width="2" />
          <text x="14" y="3" fill="#FF6685" font-family="monospace" font-size="7">YAOGAN-33 SAR</text>
        </g>

        <!-- MEO GPS Sat -->
        <g transform="translate(140, 140)" class="sat-node">
          <circle r="4" fill="#8E8FC9" />
          <rect x="-8" y="-3" width="16" height="6" fill="none" stroke="#8E8FC9" />
          <text x="14" y="3" fill="#8E8FC9" font-family="monospace" font-size="7">GPS III SV05</text>
        </g>

        <!-- GEO SBIRS Sat -->
        <g transform="translate(220, 50)" class="sat-node">
          <circle r="5" fill="#FFBE98" />
          <polygon points="0,-6 6,4 -6,4" fill="#FFBE98" />
          <text x="14" y="3" fill="#FFBE98" font-family="monospace" font-size="7">SBIRS GEO-6</text>
        </g>

        <!-- ASAT Kill Envelope Vector (Ground to LEO) -->
        <line x1="90" y1="330" x2="175" y2="240" stroke="#BB2649" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 3" />
        <polygon points="175,240 167,243 171,248" fill="#BB2649" />
        <text x="65" y="285" fill="#BB2649" font-family="monospace" font-size="7" font-weight="bold">DA-ASAT KINETIC INTERCEPTION</text>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Satellite Systems Dossier Cards -->
    <div class="space-dossier-list" id="spaceDossierList">
      <!-- Sat 1: Keyhole Optical -->
      <div class="sat-card hud-panel" data-orbit="LEO">
        <div class="sat-card-top font-mono">
          <span class="badge badge-pantone-2021">LEO • 250 - 400 KM</span>
          <span class="sat-operator">US SPACE FORCE / NRO</span>
        </div>
        <h4 class="sat-name">KH-11 KENNEN / USA-314 Class (Optical IMINT)</h4>
        <p class="sat-desc">Equipped with a 2.4-meter Hubble-class primary mirror. Delivers ground resolution of sub-0.05 meters (5 cm), allowing analysts to identify individual weapon hardpoints on parked fighter jets.</p>
        <div class="sat-threat-box font-mono">
          <span>VULNERABILITY:</span> Susceptible to Russian 'Peresvet' ground-based laser dazzling and Chinese SC-19 direct-ascent kinetic kill interceptors.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sat 2: SAR Yaogan -->
      <div class="sat-card hud-panel" data-orbit="LEO">
        <div class="sat-card-top font-mono">
          <span class="badge badge-pantone-2023">LEO • 500 - 680 KM</span>
          <span class="sat-operator">CHINA PLASSF (STRATEGIC SUPPORT FORCE)</span>
        </div>
        <h4 class="sat-name">Yaogan-33 / 34 Series (Synthetic Aperture Radar)</h4>
        <p class="sat-desc">Active microwave X-band radar imaging satellites. Pierces through heavy monsoonal cloud cover, smoke, and nighttime darkness to cue DF-21D and DF-26 anti-ship ballistic missiles against maneuvering carrier strike groups.</p>
        <div class="sat-threat-box font-mono">
          <span>CREATOR TAKEAWAY:</span> Explains why modern navies cannot hide in bad weather. Radar satellites don't need daylight to generate target-grade telemetry.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sat 3: GPS III -->
      <div class="sat-card hud-panel" data-orbit="MEO">
        <div class="sat-card-top font-mono">
          <span class="badge badge-pantone-2022">MEO • 20,200 KM</span>
          <span class="sat-operator">US SPACE FORCE (SPACE DELTA 8)</span>
        </div>
        <h4 class="sat-name">GPS Block III (Military M-Code)</h4>
        <p class="sat-desc">Next-generation PNT constellation broadcasting the high-power, cryptographic 'M-Code' signal with 8x greater anti-jamming resilience against Russian Krasukha-4 and Borisoglebsk-2 electronic warfare arrays.</p>
        <div class="sat-threat-box font-mono">
          <span>STRATEGIC IMPACT:</span> Modern precision-guided munitions (JDAM, Excalibur, Tomahawk) rely on M-Code correlation to maintain CEP under 1 meter in contested GPS environments.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sat 4: SBIRS GEO -->
      <div class="sat-card hud-panel" data-orbit="GEO">
        <div class="sat-card-top font-mono">
          <span class="badge badge-pantone-2024">GEO • 35,786 KM</span>
          <span class="sat-operator">US SPACE FORCE (SPACE DELTA 4)</span>
        </div>
        <h4 class="sat-name">SBIRS GEO-6 (Space-Based Infrared System)</h4>
        <p class="sat-desc">Persistent staring infrared sensor hovering in geostationary orbit. Detects the thermal rocket exhaust plume of intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) and hypersonic boost-glide launches within seconds of ignition.</p>
        <div class="sat-threat-box font-mono">
          <span>EARLY WARNING:</span> Provides the initial cueing data for Alaska and California Ground-based Midcourse Defense (GMD) interceptors.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll('.orbit-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.orbit-btn').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('active'));
      btn.classList.add('active');
      const orbit = btn.getAttribute('data-orbit');
      
      document.querySelectorAll('.sat-card').forEach(card => {
        const cardOrbit = card.getAttribute('data-orbit');
        card.style.display = (orbit === 'ALL' || cardOrbit === orbit) ? 'flex' : 'none';
      });
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .space-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .space-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(147, 149, 151, 0.15);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .space-title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .space-heading {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .orbit-toggles {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .orbit-btn {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .orbit-btn.active {
    background: var(--bg-card-hover);
    border-color: var(--c-pantone-2022-peri);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .space-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .orbit-visual-box {
    background: #080B0F;
    padding: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .orbit-svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 400px;
    display: block;
  }

  .space-dossier-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .sat-card {
    padding: 1.15rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    background: rgba(14, 19, 26, 0.9);
  }

  .sat-card-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .sat-name {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .sat-desc {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .sat-threat-box {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    background: rgba(8, 11, 15, 0.6);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--primary);
    color: var(--text-main);
  }
  .sat-threat-box span {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .space-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
